@page "/terms"
@namespace Ben.Web.Website.Library.Support
@inject Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptions<Ben.Data.Common.SiteIdentity> SiteOptions

@* Anonymous for the same reason /privacy is: this is the written basis for the content-rights
   answer given to Apple and for the moderation authority the feed exercises, and both are only
   worth anything on a page anybody can read without an account. Nothing here reads the signed-in
   user — see feedback_author_sees_what_visitor_cannot. *@

<PageTitle>Terms of Service — @SiteOptions.Value.Name</PageTitle>

<div class="container-fluid px-3 py-4" style="max-width:860px; margin:auto;">

    <h1 class="mb-1">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-secondary mb-4">
        The agreement between you and @SiteOptions.Value.Name, covering the website and the
        IsHaunted iPhone and iPad app. Last updated 08/30/2026.
    </p>

    <div class="card border-primary mb-4">
        <div class="card-body">
            <h2 class="h5 card-title mb-2">The short version</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Your work stays yours. By posting it here you let us show it to the people you
                aimed it at. Be lawful and decent, get permission before you record other people
                or investigate their property, and we can remove content or accounts that break
                these rules. The service comes as it is, and being about the paranormal, it
                proves nothing.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">1. Who may use it</h2>
    <p>
        You must be at least 13 years old. If you use @SiteOptions.Value.Name for a group, you
        confirm you may act for that group. You are responsible for what happens under your
        account and for keeping your sign-in to yourself.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">2. Your content stays yours</h2>
    <p>
        Everything you create or upload — posts, photos, audio, video, readings, reports, case
        notes — remains yours. We claim no ownership of any of it.
    </p>
    <p>
        So that the service can work, you give us a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free
        licence to host, store, reproduce and display your content <em>to the audience you chose
        for it</em>: a private case file to the people on that case, a group post to your group,
        a public feed post or published page to anyone. Delete something and the licence for it
        ends, except in backups for a short time and in things other people lawfully made from
        it while it was published, such as a quote of a public post.
    </p>
    <p>
        We never sell your content, never use it for advertising, and publishing something
        beyond the audience you set is done only by you or with your consent — the same rule the
        <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> makes about your information.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">3. Your responsibilities in the field</h2>
    <p>
        Paranormal investigation happens in the real world, on real property, around real
        people. You agree that:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>You have permission to be where you investigate. Trespassing is not investigation.</li>
        <li>You have the consent the law requires before recording people — audio recording
            consent laws vary by state and country, and they are your responsibility.</li>
        <li>Client work stays confidential to the case unless the client agrees otherwise. The
            platform's private-engagement protections help, but the obligation is yours.</li>
        <li>You will not present evidence as something it is not. Label what you captured
            honestly; the community and your clients rely on it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">4. Rules of conduct</h2>
    <p>Do not use @SiteOptions.Value.Name to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>harass, threaten, or target anyone — including the living occupants of allegedly
            haunted places;</li>
        <li>post content that is unlawful, sexually explicit, or gratuitously violent;</li>
        <li>publish someone's private information — a name, an address, a face — without their
            consent;</li>
        <li>impersonate a person or group, or misrepresent who you are;</li>
        <li>spam, scrape, probe, overload, or interfere with the service or other people's use
            of it;</li>
        <li>charge vulnerable people for services you know to be baseless. Investigation is
            welcome here; exploitation is not.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">5. Moderation, and what we may remove</h2>
    <p>
        You can report any feed post, and block any user — blocking takes effect for you
        immediately. Reports go to a moderator. We may remove content, restrict features, or
        close accounts that break these terms, with or without notice, and we may preserve and
        disclose content where the law requires it. We are not obliged to monitor everything,
        and a post being visible is not our endorsement of it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">6. Groups, clients and payments</h2>
    <p>
        Groups manage their own membership, cases and clients; the group you join or hire is
        responsible for its own conduct and its own agreements with you. Paid subscriptions for
        groups are billed by @SiteOptions.Value.Name on the website, with the price and what it
        covers shown before you pay. Subscriptions are not bought inside the iPhone or iPad app.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">7. No promises about the paranormal</h2>
    <p>
        The instruments here measure real, ordinary things — magnetic fields, sound, position —
        and the app tells you exactly what they are and are not. Neither the readings nor
        anything published on this service is a claim that any place is haunted, that any
        phenomenon is paranormal, or that any evidence proves anything. Entertainment,
        investigation and community — not certification.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">8. The service comes as it is</h2>
    <p>
        We provide @SiteOptions.Value.Name "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any
        kind, and we may change, suspend or discontinue features. To the fullest extent the law
        allows, our liability to you is limited to the amount you paid us in the twelve months
        before the claim, and we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses — including
        anything that happens on an investigation. Nothing here limits liability that the law
        does not allow to be limited.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">9. Leaving, and being asked to leave</h2>
    <p>
        You can <a href="/privacy">delete your account</a> at any time, from the app or by
        asking us; what you authored for a group stays with that group, no longer under your
        name, as the privacy policy describes. We may suspend or close accounts that break these
        terms. Sections 2, 7 and 8 survive account closure.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">10. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
        If we change these terms in a way that matters, we will say so on the site before the
        change takes effect. Using the service after that is acceptance of the new terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">11. Questions</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
        The <a href="/contact">contact form</a> reaches us — no account needed. These terms are
        governed by the laws of the State of Tennessee, United States.
    </p>

</div>
